From fd23713f1f66a7dca4e23291fb2f6cf2cb32d10a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lina <lokinyauv@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 02:29:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(windows): stop scanning while preloading known base
 stations

Starting the 10s advertisement scan at startup (InitBluetooth) made
the radio scan concurrently while preloadBaseStations was enumerating
GATT services on already-known stations. On Windows this made service
discovery hang indefinitely, leaving devices stuck on "Connecting..."
forever.

Split adapter bring-up (EnableBluetooth) from starting a scan, and
only enable the adapter at startup. Scanning for new devices is still
available on demand via StartScanFor10Seconds.

(cherry picked from commit 5ddb437d30ab4c7c78d7f0fd34eaca5a5cffbebe)
